TITLE:: Probe
summary:: Real-time audio visualization, instrumentation, and signal tracing suite for SuperCollider
categories:: GUI>Visuals
related:: Guides/Probe-Visuals-and-Representation-Suite, Classes/ProbeSpectralDashboard, Classes/ProbeBandAnalyzer, Classes/ProbeInspector

DESCRIPTION::
Probe is a professional, high-performance real-time audio visualization and instrumentation suite for SuperCollider.
It provides precision oscilloscopes with zero-crossing stationary trigger edge locking, logarithmic/linear FFT spectrum analyzers with multi-mode views, ITU-R BS.1770 loudness metering, transparent in-graph signal tracing (link::Classes/UGen#-trace::), multi-preset advanced spectral dashboards, and static DSP graph inspection.

Probe maintains strict non-interference with vanilla SuperCollider core methods (link::Classes/Server#-meter::, link::Classes/Server#-scope::, link::Classes/Server#-freqscope:: are unchanged).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: version
Returns the current Probe suite version string.

METHOD:: meter
Opens a vertical server meter.
argument:: server
The target server.
argument:: numIns
Number of input channels.
argument:: numOuts
Number of output channels.
argument:: theme
Theme symbol.
argument:: density
Visual density (\micro, \compact, \extended).
argument:: meterStyle
Meter style (\dualRuler, etc.).

METHOD:: scope
Opens a precision oscilloscope with trigger edge stabilization.
argument:: server
Target server.
argument:: busIndex
Audio bus to monitor.
argument:: numChannels
Channel count.
argument:: theme
Visual theme.
argument:: rate
\audio or \control.
argument:: style
\tracks (vertically separated channels, default), \overlay (superimposed channels), or \xy.
argument:: bufSize
Oscilloscope buffer size (default 4096).
argument:: engine
Rendering engine: \smooth (default, hardware antialiased vector renderer) or \native (ScopeView blit).
argument:: lineWidth
Vector stroke width in pixels (default 1.8).
argument:: fill
Boolean indicating whether to render translucent ribbon fill (default false).

METHOD:: freqscope
Opens a precision FFT spectrum analyzer with 3-mode switching (\line, \bands, \spectrogram).
argument:: server
Target server.
argument:: busIndex
Audio bus to monitor.
argument:: fftSize
FFT size (default 2048).
argument:: theme
Visual theme.
argument:: dbRange
Decibel dynamic range (default 96).
argument:: freqMode
0 for linear, 1 for logarithmic.

METHOD:: spectrum
